Z||000000||Dan86gt3.8||11-23-2001||04:57 AM||||Ya my front clip is a bit messed up and I do not have the time for a repaint, plus i cant seem to keep the bugs from slaming into my car so I figured its time for a bra!  I was gona ask for one for christmas.  <P>So what fits the best?  Which is made the best (ie last;s the longest,  does not rip up or fade)??<P>any info would be great! <P>btw- it is for a 86 gt<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>1/4- 15.3@90mph<BR>Aim-deekbandit||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indy-2M4||11-23-2001||07:34 AM||||I was gonna say NONE until I saw that your front end is in need of paint. As soon as you get her painted, let her go braless!||||reg||1
Z||000002||firstfiero||11-23-2001||09:32 AM||||    I had two. The one from the fiero store and the I now have a calgon bra. The calgon bra cost more but The fit is perfect. The wolf bra from the fiero store fit like crap.<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||deceler8||11-23-2001||10:12 AM||||Someone is always selling Covercraft bras on EBAY...I got one for $22.<P>These only cover the front fascia...don't overlap the hood or headlights, so no hood opening or headlight hassles.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/deceler8_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||REDHOTT88||11-23-2001||10:56 AM||||I just got a "Wolf" bra from the fiero store.<BR>I hate it! Doesn't fit good at all! <P>You can see my bra-burning crusade in the "technical forum"   HaHa!<P><P>------------------<BR>1988 Formula (red & shiny allover)- and she doesn't like to wear a bra!||||reg||4
Z||000005||Dan86gt3.8||11-23-2001||12:39 PM||||Sweet so I am thionking not to get the one from the fiero store.  Should I go to the local autozone or pepboys and get thier brand?<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>1/4- 15.3@90mph<BR>Aim-deekbandit||||reg||1
Z||000006||REDHOTT88||11-23-2001||12:50 PM||||I think if you do buy a bra, you should keep the reciept.<P>They look good in the store but, need to be fitted on your car, and then make the final judgement.<P>I've heard from several posts in my "hate the bra" post in the technical forum from a couple days ago that the Le-bra is alright.<P>But as for me, my baby is going to remain "braless. Her headlights are just too sexy!<BR><P>------------------<BR>1988 Formula <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (red & shiny allover)</FONT>- and she doesn't like to wear a bra!||||reg||12
Z||000007||Dan86gt3.8||11-23-2001||08:11 PM||||Well I have never ben a huge fan of bras but, if I got one it would hide a bunch of flaws<BR>a. horible flakin/ spiderweb from hitting a 45 degree incline<BR>b. the hood and the bumper cover do not line up because of a wreck<BR>c. I have so damn bugs that will not come out<BR>d. am missing the fiero emblem<P>so instead of having to take of the ocver sand on it for like nine days having to go buy more paint then the hastle of putting the damn thing back on and trying to get it to line up, and buyiongt that eblem, I will just put a bra on it!<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>1/4- 15.3@90mph<BR>Aim-deekbandit||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fformula88||11-23-2001||10:26 PM||||My father's 85 SE came with a LeBra on it.  Although it generally is not on the car, it does look good and seems to be holding up.  I am not sure how new it is, but its not real new.<P>I also have a LeBra for my Ford Probe.  I am not too impressed with the fit, but it has held up decently.  I use it for highway trips to protect from bugs and stones, and it does the job.  <P>Ovrall I'd rate them ok, not great.  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Haze_Performance||11-23-2001||11:35 PM||||Heres my 2 cents.... LeBra 100%. Most of the others have that little guard on the top...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">  Not my thing..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlife.gif">    <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="purple">Goto Website - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000010||overlord||11-24-2001||10:26 PM||||i have a wolf bra (i think).  Couldnt find any names anywhere on the packaging.<P>but anywyas i agree it did NOT fit very well..  But after several attempts, it finally got "the shape" of the front end...and now fits  perfect everytime.<P>i was so close to tossing it in the garbage, after so many times taking it on and off on and off, i guess it stretched it to the right shape.||||reg||1
